        <headline>Flash Flood Warning issued September 26 at 12:09AM MDT until September 26 at 2:15AM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM</headline>
        <description>At 1209 AM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing heavy
rain across the warned area. Between 2 and 3.5 inches of rain have
fallen. Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are possible in the
warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.

HAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing
flash flooding.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams, urban
areas, highways, streets and underpasses.

Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...
Grady and Wheatland.

Flash flooding is likely along Highway 275 east of Wheatland as well
as  Highways 209 and 469 near Grady.
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.

Be especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the
dangers of flooding.</instruction>
